Subject: [PATCH] max31785: return one byte for STATUS_FANS_1_2

STATUS_FANS_1_2 is a byte register. Sending a word leaves a byte in
PMBusDevice.out_buf after a normal SMBus byte read. The next word read
then consumes that stale byte before the fan speed response.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/hw/sensor/max31785.c
+++ b/hw/sensor/max31785.c
@@ -192,5 +192,5 @@
     case PMBUS_STATUS_FANS_1_2:
         if (pmdev->page <= MAX31785_MAX_FAN_PAGE) {
-            pmbus_send16(pmdev, pmdev->pages[pmdev->page].status_fans_1_2);
+            pmbus_send8(pmdev, pmdev->pages[pmdev->page].status_fans_1_2);
         }
         break;

